<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>21 Savage Fans</title>
  <link rel="shortcut icon" href="favicon.ico">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="font-awesome.min.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
  <h1>21 Savage</h1>
  <h2>Why you trappin so hard?</h2>


  <h3>Messages</h3>
  <ul class="messages">
  <%# The server runs this template (res.render in GET /) and passes in `messages`,
      the array of documents from MongoDB. The loop builds one <li> per message.
      The "percent-equals" tags below print a value into the HTML, escaped, so user
      text can't inject HTML. Comments like this one ("percent-hash" tags) are
      stripped by EJS and never reach the browser. %>
  <% for(var i=0; i<messages.length; i++) {%>
    <%# I gave each span a class name (name, msg, thumbUpCount, thumbDownCount) so
        main.js can find it with li.querySelector('.name'). The old code found values
        by position (childNodes[1], [3], [5]), which silently grabs the wrong element
        as soon as a span is added, like the thumbDownCount span I added.
        thumbDownCount is new: thumbDown was saved in MongoDB but never displayed.
        `|| 0` shows 0 when a message has no stored count. Older messages may not have
        a thumbDown field, and without || 0 they would show a blank instead.
        data-id stores the message's unique MongoDB _id on the <li>, so main.js can tell
        the server exactly which message was clicked. Name + text weren't enough: two
        messages can have the same text, and the browser's innerText changes some text
        (double spaces become one, a missing msg becomes ""), so the wrong message got
        the vote or no message matched (404). %>
    <li class="message" data-id="<%= messages[i]._id %>">
      <span class="name"><%= messages[i].name %></span>
      <span class="msg"><%= messages[i].msg %></span>
      <span class="thumbUpCount"><%= messages[i].thumbUp || 0 %></span>
      <span><i class="fa fa-thumbs-up" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
      <span class="thumbDownCount"><%= messages[i].thumbDown || 0 %></span>
      <span><i class="fa fa-thumbs-down" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
      <span><i class="fa fa-trash" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
    </li>
  <% } %>
  </ul>

  <h2>Add a message</h2>

  <form action="/messages" method="POST">
    <input type="text" placeholder="name" name="name">
    <input type="text" placeholder="message" name="msg">
    <button type="submit">Submit</button>
  </form>

  <script src="main.js"></script>

</body>
</html>
